 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "megillah.24a.5",
   "daf": "24a",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "מְדַלְּגִין בַּנָּבִיא וְאֵין מְדַלְּגִין בַּתּוֹרָה. וּרְמִינְהִי: קוֹרֵא ״אַחֲרֵי מוֹת״ וְ״אַךְ בֶּעָשׂוֹר״ — וְהָא קָא מְדַלֵּג!",
   "en": "§ We learned further in the mishna: «One may skip» from one place to another while reading «the Prophets, but one may not skip» from one place to another while reading «the Torah.» The Gemara «raises a contradiction» from a mishna (Yoma 68b): On Yom Kippur, the High Priest «reads» the section beginning with the verse: «“After the death”» (Leviticus 16:1), and then he reads the section beginning with the verse: «“Only on the tenth day”» (Leviticus 23:27). «Doesn’t he skip» from the first section to the second section?"
  }
